    tc: "O(L) per operation",
    sc: "O(total characters)",
    sig: "<b>Signal:</b> autocomplete, spell-check, 'does any word start with…', or repeated prefix queries over a fixed dictionary. Also any problem where a hash set of words is <em>almost</em> right but you need prefixes.",
    why: "Each node is one character; the path from the root spells the prefix. Lookup costs the length of the word, <b>independent of how many words are stored</b> — that is the property a hash set cannot give you, because hashing needs the whole key and tells you nothing about prefixes.",
    trap: "<b><code>search</code> and <code>startsWith</code> differ by exactly one line.</b> <code>search</code> must check the <code>is_end</code> flag; <code>startsWith</code> must not. Returning 'node exists' for <code>search</code> makes every prefix look like a stored word — passes the sample, fails the hidden tests.",
    say: "Each node is a character, lookup is O(word length) regardless of dictionary size, and the end-of-word flag is what separates a stored word from a mere prefix.",
    py: "class Trie:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.root = {}                  # dict-of-dicts is fine and fast\n\n    def insert(self, w):\n        node = self.root\n        for ch in w:\n            node = node.setdefault(ch, {})\n        node['#'] = True                # end-of-word marker\n\n    def _walk(self, s):\n        node = self.root\n        for ch in s:\n            if ch not in node:\n                return None\n            node = node[ch]\n        return node\n\n    def search(self, w):\n        n = self._walk(w)\n        return n is not None and '#' in n     # MUST check the flag\n\n    def startsWith(self, p):\n        return self._walk(p) is not None      # must NOT check it",
    cpp: "struct Node {\n    Node* kid[26] = {};\n    bool end = false;\n};\n\nclass Trie {\n    Node* root = new Node();\n    Node* walk(const string& s) {\n        Node* n = root;\n        for (char c : s) {\n            if (!n->kid[c - 'a']) return nullptr;\n            n = n->kid[c - 'a'];\n        }\n        return n;\n    }\npublic:\n    void insert(const string& w) {\n        Node* n = root;\n        for (char c : w) {\n            if (!n->kid[c - 'a']) n->kid[c - 'a'] = new Node();\n            n = n->kid[c - 'a'];\n        }\n        n->end = true;\n    }\n    bool search(const string& w)     { Node* n = walk(w); return n && n->end; }\n    bool startsWith(const string& p) { return walk(p) != nullptr; }\n};",
    java: "class Trie {\n    private static class Node {\n        Node[] kid = new Node[26];\n        boolean end;\n    }\n    private final Node root = new Node();\n\n    private Node walk(String s) {\n        Node n = root;\n        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {\n            if (n.kid[c - 'a'] == null) return null;\n            n = n.kid[c - 'a'];\n        }\n        return n;\n    }\n    public void insert(String w) {\n        Node n = root;\n        for (char c : w.toCharArray()) {\n            if (n.kid[c - 'a'] == null) n.kid[c - 'a'] = new Node();\n            n = n.kid[c - 'a'];\n        }\n        n.end = true;\n    }\n    public boolean search(String w)     { Node n = walk(w); return n != null && n.end; }\n    public boolean startsWith(String p) { return walk(p) != null; }\n}",
